@tradition sowing
// Sowing morning: the first Saturday of each season (days 6, 97, 188, 279), late morning in the garden. Everyone plants
// a seedling; yours (day 6, your first weekend) grows as long as you're aboard. The seasons designer's (seat 17) from
// wave 1b; first written by the traditions engineer as the format's sample. On days 6 and 188 the harvest morning
// (09:30-11:30, every other Saturday) comes first, so the texts never say "after the harvest": on days 97 and 279 there
// isn't one. Design note: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md.
k: 434
title: Sowing morning
when: quarter week 1 saturday
at: 11:45-12:40
min: 20
prio: 1
where: 3 pool garden
hold: none
who: tomas always, cruz-tove always, gardener 90%, garden-lover 75%, everyone 30%
anim: water
host: cruz-tove
from: brennan
ties: garden sow
trace: seedlingYours
invite: host=tomas odds=50% line="Sowing morning at quarter to twelve. Come and plant one. I'll show you which end goes down."

== mail
- A new season starts in the garden: Sowing morning tomorrow, {time}. Everyone plants a seedling. Yours grows as long as you're aboard.

== ask
- Sowing morning today. Bring clean hands.
- I'm planting basil this time. Don't tell Brennan, she'll want it.   #funny
- A new season in the garden. I always plant something new.
- Sowing at quarter to twelve. Tove says there are enough pots for everyone.

== here
- Two seeds a pot. One for luck.
- Gently. They're only small.   #warm
- Write your name on the tag, or Tove will name it for you.   #funny
- Mine from last season is the tall one at the end. Look at it go.

== thanks
- You press a seedling into its pot and write your name on the tag. {season} has begun.
- You plant a seedling with the others and set it under the lamps. It's tiny, and it's yours.   #warm

== chatter
- Whose seedling is that, already leaning towards the lamps?   #funny
- I've planted one every season since I came aboard. It's a little row of me now.   #warm
- Sowing morning on Saturday. The garden smells of wet soil for days after.
